<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:27:30Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-all" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Intelligent women get less help at work, study finds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0247ab6596a4299f7a2290f89f1588dd5507abd31df17d27d28ae87ad7e8d326</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:27:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/intelligent-women-get-less-help-at-work-study-finds/a-79910881--d3f9551f1647.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/intelligent-women-get-less-help-at-work-study-finds/a-79910881?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Women who scored high on intelligence tests were seen as more hostile by their teammates and got less help, a new study finds. High-scoring men faced no such penalty. Research explains why.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>India news : Modi government approves $340 million museum in Delhi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4478358cd96bec8b5450714fdce8f6ca373b59e46746bb1369a28c353c40aaf1</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:27:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T06:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-modi-government-approves-340-million-museum-in-delhi/live-79925477--8b8209e9e65a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-modi-government-approves-340-million-museum-in-delhi/live-79925477?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The government says that the 'Yuge Yugeen Bharat Museum' will have the world's "largest" museum dispaly area." DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine peace talks: US envoys arrive in Russia to meet with Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:459dba99da0c0faa70391462ec1e4f60e3c844851cadc4eb1b0ecbc22bdfc0b9</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:27:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T06:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-peace-talks-us-envoys-arrive-in-russia-to-meet-with-putin/live-79925580--ee5fd1bf3562.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-peace-talks-us-envoys-arrive-in-russia-to-meet-with-putin/live-79925580?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US president's son-in-law Jared Kushner and envoy Steve Witkoff are in Russia to meet Vladimir Putin. The expected meeting comes after two days of trilateral talks in Abu Dhabi. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Where the US's war with Iran stands after the midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:587685184e5587be762ebe90d2befe160e4288bccf274c752209ce09bee91cf7</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:27:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T05:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/where-the-us-s-war-with-iran-stands-after-the-midterms/a-79918176--06fb494a8763.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/where-the-us-s-war-with-iran-stands-after-the-midterms/a-79918176?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Almost nine months after it began, the war in Iran has calmed to the point where Donald Trump sees an end. But with the key issues of the conflict unresolved and political change in the US, what is the situation?</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo XIV returns to Peru to a big welcome, calls it his 'homeland'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:054488695774494a8381946266bf008420ffc8e8f44ce6b90607fa6435b81581</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:27:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T04:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-xiv-returns-to-peru-to-a-big-welcome-calls-it-his-homeland/a-79925466--9266e872124f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-xiv-returns-to-peru-to-a-big-welcome-calls-it-his-homeland/a-79925466?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An estimated 3 million people greeted Pope Leo XIV in Lima as the Peruvian-citizen pontiff began a six-day homecoming visit to the country where he spent two decades as a missionary and bishop.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia board reportedly weighs ousting Huang amid alleged affairs with exec and suspected Chinese spy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ec5dcafae74fc092aa4a12f0737e4dc484ec3ae3cffb1b1618deba162c76829</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:27:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T00:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nvidia-board-reportedly-weighs-ousting-huang-amid-alleged-affairs-with-exec-and-suspected-chinese-sp/a-79925002--9cb9fa6427a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nvidia-board-reportedly-weighs-ousting-huang-amid-alleged-affairs-with-exec-and-suspected-chinese-spy/a-79925002?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia's board is reportedly preparing to oust Jensen Huang amid reports of an affair with a suspected Chinese spy. The shake-up would leave the world's leading AI chip supplier without the co-founder who built it.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Mississippi Senate race: Democrat Scott Colom defeats Republican Cindy Hyde-Smith</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a0979889448ebe4e720104d372fb004a52f3573ac5a739708a6cae4d99d4765</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:27:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T23:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mississippi-senate-race-democrat-scott-colom-defeats-republican-cindy-hyde-smith/a-79924938--fc149241f06d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mississippi-senate-race-democrat-scott-colom-defeats-republican-cindy-hyde-smith/a-79924938?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The southern US state of Mississippi has elected its first Black senator in more than 140 years. Democrat Scott Colom has won the seat in a historic upset, according to projections.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russian Foreign Ministry says its ambassador to US has died</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae2823e4e785c82a42243bbb0d65a7760fd2d7d79ad730a1fb3a8d4b1fbe32e2</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:27:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T23:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-foreign-ministry-says-its-ambassador-to-us-has-died/a-79924829--521886c8847c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-foreign-ministry-says-its-ambassador-to-us-has-died/a-79924829?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's Foreign Ministry has said that Alexander Darchiev died from a chronic illness at the age of 66. The long-time diplomat had been in the Washington post since early 2025.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Spain: Housing crisis prompts general strike, mass nighttime protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e1893c00d6cd3235c7f741e33edfdba8aac289ecb299894f4406368210372078</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T21:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-housing-crisis-prompts-general-strike-mass-nighttime-protests/a-79915208--fc6d9d65a508.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-housing-crisis-prompts-general-strike-mass-nighttime-protests/a-79915208?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of thousands of citizens have hit the streets to protest Spain's housing crisis after millions of union workers staged a general strike. The crisis has triggered snap elections to take place on November 29.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Fears of rising antisemitism in Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b14c5f375330736f6b4789a8696fedb7c1290d71f88ba5e26aefb7818ee9b0ec</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T20:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fears-of-rising-antisemitism-in-europe/a-79921783--20638e7d2425.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fears-of-rising-antisemitism-in-europe/a-79921783?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Holocaust survivor Regina Sluszny commemorates the victims of Auschwitz as Jewish communities across Europe face growing hostility. What does the promise of "Never Again" mean for Jewish life in Europe today?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>VW scraps production modernization plan citing tough financial straits</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:727fab8b15c6cf6bf395da1e7da9e5d5b0fe570b967d14fbc4d7f4e3ca044be4</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T19:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/vw-scraps-production-modernization-plan-citing-tough-financial-straits/a-79923597--b06c676e46e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/vw-scraps-production-modernization-plan-citing-tough-financial-straits/a-79923597?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">VW has announced that it will scrap large-scale modernization in light of its current economic situation. Employee representatives accuse leadership of putting short-term profits before long-term company viability.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Integration of immigrants in Germany: Much has been accomplished but problems remain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a85540c771f6d92a7c09c3509c0eff32a18464fa888972baa7f6b1380d761c8</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T17:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/integration-of-immigrants-in-germany-much-has-been-accomplished-but-problems-remain/a-79923241--cdefd1e9fff8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/integration-of-immigrants-in-germany-much-has-been-accomplished-but-problems-remain/a-79923241?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Federal office for Migration and Refugees has released a new Integration Report. It found that while the integration of people with a migrant history is improving, violent youth remain a problem.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Democracy study: One-quarter of Germans want a right-wing authoritarian dictatorship</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e4063feaa37b95f2344431b1fb4510afe18964b91f3a660da7723ee0e18bced</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/democracy-study-one-quarter-of-germans-want-a-right-wing-authoritarian-dictatorship/a-79922718--e6377f13d887.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/democracy-study-one-quarter-of-germans-want-a-right-wing-authoritarian-dictatorship/a-79922718?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right AfD's electoral successes point to a new trend in Germany: Prejudice, resentment, and extremism are on the rise. A new study suggests satisfaction with democracy is at a low ebb.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya's last Ebola patient leaves hospital</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c898b150cff0fb85b79643f17291a7b45adccb5b056b4cb99265aa2c4e7a53b1</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T16:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kenya-s-last-ebola-patient-leaves-hospital/a-79921240--e9705d91e6bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kenya-s-last-ebola-patient-leaves-hospital/a-79921240?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Kenya had nine confirmed cases, while DR Congo continues to battle its deadliest outbreak of the disease.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil electoral court fines Meta, sees no deliberate election bias</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a7f84dedaf85e07df38c7094f09fc1f222eceaef08ad333b0a099460ec38fd4b</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-electoral-court-fines-meta-sees-no-deliberate-election-bias/a-79920780--215a8f08f312.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-electoral-court-fines-meta-sees-no-deliberate-election-bias/a-79920780?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The fine came after President Lula's coalition filed a complaint. The court said there was no evidence of intent to influence the election. Meta said it will defend itself against "false allegations."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is AIIB's complaint mechanism failing affected communities?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:29ede6cd734494378a8f4c971c9f497ea709237fa3b817bd1992d64a4a31a4e0</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917--1bfa788b7764.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AIIB has a grievance redress mechanism for people affected by projects it finances. But those seeking to file a complaint face significant hurdles. Critics say reforms and greater transparency are needed.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73d0619a382e74160b32972aa754da9864d6588d4bfd94febd76083d64af9303</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Italy: Hundreds of schools evacuated after bomb threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:420dce806d7537c214a03884489feab7b4958ee5dd513359096b87ffbb89cf55</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T13:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/italy-hundreds-of-schools-evacuated-after-bomb-threats/a-79918034--3d07ea5d3a16.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/italy-hundreds-of-schools-evacuated-after-bomb-threats/a-79918034?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Although the government believes the threat to be a hoax, it has nevertheless prompted concerns about "hybrid warfare" in Europe. Similar messages were sent in Northern Ireland, Ireland, and Bulgaria.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Tundu Lissu: After escaping the death penalty, what does his guilty verdict mean for Tanzania's democracy?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4adfb6be844827b73bcf5289aa518b35f187c1a2a7798bd3fbd2682b362f8cc7</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T13:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tundu-lissu-after-escaping-the-death-penalty-what-does-his-guilty-verdict-mean-for-tanzania-s-democr/a-79908512--3044020567d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tundu-lissu-after-escaping-the-death-penalty-what-does-his-guilty-verdict-mean-for-tanzania-s-democracy/a-79908512?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A treason trial could have meant death by hanging for Tanzanian opposition leader Tundu Lissu. Instead, he now faces four years in prison for incitement to unrest. Can voices of dissident truly be heard in the country?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Only 1/3 of Germans satisfied with state of democracy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5617e5b708775e9a49d162ae70f4ef53d2ea46489f597585012b8fef9575a2ca</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T11:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-only-1-3-of-germans-satisfied-with-state-of-democracy/live-79915066--348a315bae46.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-only-1-3-of-germans-satisfied-with-state-of-democracy/live-79915066?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new authoritarianism study has revealed a new low in satisfaction levels with the functioning of German democracy. Meanwhile, the Bundeswehr has banned Chinese-made drones. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>DW Science explainer on the default mode network: what your brain does when you aren't focusing on anything, and why it's important.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cd8bc2d8fdb89df65f8cf6bdf90cadfda7c218a7b38436fb33bb4d9c5c60c6e</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T06:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dw-science-explainer-on-the-default-mode-network-what-your-brain-does-when-you-aren-t-focusing-on-an/a-79908787--cf91bcf53b1d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dw-science-explainer-on-the-default-mode-network-what-your-brain-does-when-you-aren-t-focusing-on-anything-and-why-it-s-important/a-79908787?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Doing nothing might be the ultimate brain hack. When you're bored, the brain goes into default mode network. It's not only healthy for you, but it may also shape the very essence of your identity.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Germany slips in climate protection rankings as other countries make gains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3aba3bb788085b93e71965ea0533d98eba0ac5e42140035a4904bfd9aaca3d2a</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T06:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-slips-in-climate-protection-rankings-as-other-countries-make-gains/a-79913635--edb7d622928e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-slips-in-climate-protection-rankings-as-other-countries-make-gains/a-79913635?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Record renewable energy growth is driving climate progress in some countries, but Germany and many major emitters are falling behind.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>British counterterrorism police arrest US soldier accused of spying on behalf of Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e49f5bbe7d79dcb569520ded634a041c0d3a71b660e9c0834d1057844316bee</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T19:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/british-counterterrorism-police-arrest-us-soldier-accused-of-spying-on-behalf-of-russia/a-79913240--5991e0a904a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/british-counterterrorism-police-arrest-us-soldier-accused-of-spying-on-behalf-of-russia/a-79913240?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A member of the US Army has been arrested near Gloucester in England. Police said he was suspected of espionage activity in connection with Russia. Investigators from the US and UK are involved in the probe.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK Privy Council overrules Trinidad and Tobago gay sex law</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10f240614f2f911e59245f83bd8a86ac1d4b692ff7b5a1dcb50bb3161bac1fda</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T19:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-privy-council-overrules-trinidad-and-tobago-gay-sex-law/a-79912163--f186aba38925.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-privy-council-overrules-trinidad-and-tobago-gay-sex-law/a-79912163?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A London court has overturned a Trinidad and Tobago law criminalizing consensual sexual relations between male same-sex couples. As a result of the colonial legacy, it is the independent country's last court of appeal.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Victims of Nazi war in Poland call on Germany for support</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b1e897a4f099f4641fa7dfba41d3dfaf41c6a52b7a39cd66075efe1a45e5da4</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T17:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/victims-of-nazi-war-in-poland-call-on-germany-for-support/a-79909311--36756d6320e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/victims-of-nazi-war-in-poland-call-on-germany-for-support/a-79909311?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than 80 years after the end of World War II, Polish victims of the Nazi regime are still waiting for a "humanitarian gesture" from Germany. The 2027 draft budget hasn't left them much hope for possible reparations.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran denies role in fridge hack, France summons ambassador</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86155543decb5df7bd763d31769a1f93154b7943b5ed4818f32a66dcfacecd56</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-denies-role-in-fridge-hack-france-summons-ambassador/a-79910206--6d0355211a72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-denies-role-in-fridge-hack-france-summons-ambassador/a-79910206?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France has said it rules "nothing" out in response to a cyberattack on supermarket refrigeration units. Iran, however, said it categorically rejected Paris' "baseless and one-sided accusations" of IRGC involvement.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Controversial kinship: From colonial rule to the Holocaust?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5928c786253c35dfacbdafb9ba0fd02bf1288b2b586408f4b16d8b831eb8bc61</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228--16129c6452e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hitler once called Eastern Europe "Germany's India." A new exhibition examines the links between colonialism and Nazism, and the bitter debate over where comparisons illuminate history and where they fall short.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Neuer injury gives Urbig chance to shape Bayern and Germany future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:edc2d50430b91ea26bde9293bfd6273866f84b54fae3a1276eaee49c3c756a56</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042--b0a77bac4246.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Manuel Neuer's latest injury gives Jonas Urbig a run of games in Bayern's goal. Marc-André ter Stegen remains Germany’s No. 1, but Urbig now has a chance to strengthen his case for the future.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Megaspeed and the battle to go high-end Nvidia chips into China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8653c746808904868fed3882a9f8a5c2a78398ac19451a9650f120656140eb5f</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T14:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/megaspeed-and-the-battle-to-go-high-end-nvidia-chips-into-china/a-79909129--5e400fbb45fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/megaspeed-and-the-battle-to-go-high-end-nvidia-chips-into-china/a-79909129?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang's affair with a suspected Chinese spy has shone a light on Megaspeed, the company she worked for. It is under investigation in the US for smuggling Nvidia chips into China, which it denies.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria highway pileup kills 12, dozens injured: PM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:83698520e146387a4147e4732784548268f1271cd2f2195bb16a3ad7421b3645</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T11:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-highway-pileup-kills-12-dozens-injured-pm/a-79907978--e4c51329b4c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-highway-pileup-kills-12-dozens-injured-pm/a-79907978?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least 12 people were killed and dozens injured in a series of crashes caused by thick fog in Bulgaria. Police, firefighters and paramedics were dispatched to the scene for the rescue operation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Borussia Dortmund's Felix Nmecha and the question of religion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f36120b23d51b59c691959a355ce2fb95d9d7fcaab26725215f7da06aeffad83</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T11:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-s-felix-nmecha-and-the-question-of-religion/a-79900432--cd7bb6e11389.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-s-felix-nmecha-and-the-question-of-religion/a-79900432?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Felix Nmecha's "Crowns down" celebration has drawn criticism from a Borussia Dortmund fan club, reopening debate over faith, inclusion and religious messaging in football.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Online disinformation rife after Krakow mass shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32898ceef6cedef953432677f7cb5f64978737d4c32ad7f24d66d56c981d45b2</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T10:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-online-disinformation-rife-after-krakow-mass-shooting/a-79900620--80ad1afffb68.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-online-disinformation-rife-after-krakow-mass-shooting/a-79900620?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fake and AI-manipulated images spread online in the hours after the Krakow attack, fueling false narratives about the mass shooting. DW Fact Check examined what's real, and what isn't.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why electrification is the climate game changer we need</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cede6bf2b4894e6745a515b8505919b8b5d3031b2cc25334785cbadff5623d6</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-electrification-is-the-climate-game-changer-we-need/a-79615979--0dbca6445640.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-electrification-is-the-climate-game-changer-we-need/a-79615979?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From EVs and electric buses on the road, heat pumps warming homes and solar panels powering appliances, the shift to electrifying tech is already in full swing. But what exactly does "electrification" mean?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Will Australia push for fossil fuel exit at UN talks?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd8e67dd000aa4476b1751f009c2154feec11020adaecfa373fde55e2b38cf3c</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T07:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-australia-push-for-fossil-fuel-exit-at-un-talks/a-79782066--e866c53d355a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-australia-push-for-fossil-fuel-exit-at-un-talks/a-79782066?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The heat is on Australia as chief negotiator at the COP31 UN climate conference to forge a path away from coal and gas, and to protect Pacific neighbors facing rising sea levels.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>US, Russia, Ukraine wrap up talks with prisoner exchange agreement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7f4d621bda98ffe396c8548cf3acda872cfa83b450906829710efc41c334b067</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:27:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T07:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-russia-ukraine-wrap-up-talks-with-prisoner-exchange-agreement/live-79906232--00cfe2e7daba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-russia-ukraine-wrap-up-talks-with-prisoner-exchange-agreement/live-79906232?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Peace talks between Russia, Ukraine and the US concluded in the United Arab Emirates. The two day talks were the first such meeting since February. DW has the latest updates.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why malnutrition can go unnoticed, and what that means for our health</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:289e347ffd05bf0f96cc5338cc60aedbb18fccf5894845eb2f35769ebea8a417</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T05:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-malnutrition-can-go-unnoticed-and-what-that-means-for-our-health/a-79871016--a7247c0af1e5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-malnutrition-can-go-unnoticed-and-what-that-means-for-our-health/a-79871016?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than 2 billion people worldwide suffer from nutrient deficiencies, most of them in the Global South. The health consequences can be devastating.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Iran war oil shock drives dip in global emissions, study shows</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:595ce7e3f11005c14da7419966a94e51722805c317a717d128306f9b2d7947eb</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T03:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-war-oil-shock-drives-dip-in-global-emissions-study-shows/a-79905937--fec20d5dba18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-oil-shock-drives-dip-in-global-emissions-study-shows/a-79905937?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Global carbon emissions are expected to fall slightly in 2026, but not because of major progress on climate action. Instead, it's high energy prices following the US attack on Iran that's driving the trend.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>New trilateral talks on Ukraine war in Abu Dhabi: What to expect?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2b58bee2963ed9de67b31a5fc2cd1a35a15ad287367e598c270f5c918a048c3</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T23:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-trilateral-talks-on-ukraine-war-in-abu-dhabi-what-to-expect/a-79905734--3c6da76b72e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-trilateral-talks-on-ukraine-war-in-abu-dhabi-what-to-expect/a-79905734?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian and Russian representatives last met in February for talks on ending the war, but the same sticking points remain. Ukraine continues to demand security guarantees, which is a non-starter for Russia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia: Independent Novaya Gazeta shuts its Moscow newsroom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a81d5d08c63e38209233d5ad30a4179b381b1d584934d78afc17815e1df826b6</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-independent-novaya-gazeta-shuts-its-moscow-newsroom/a-79899827--d187f3fbc3fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-independent-novaya-gazeta-shuts-its-moscow-newsroom/a-79899827?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The investigative newspaper is closing its doors after Russian authorities labeled it a "foreign agent" and ordered it vacate its Moscow premises.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's ice hockey team says Russia replacing it at World Juniors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a039c2928504087300fe2c2066c1425ba1deed72c91fb893bbfab81bfc988232</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-ice-hockey-team-says-russia-replacing-it-at-world-juniors/a-79901844--43300d3ba1be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-ice-hockey-team-says-russia-replacing-it-at-world-juniors/a-79901844?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The wrangling over Russia's return to international ice hockey continues, with Norway saying it has been kicked out of the next major tournament to accommodate Russia. Switzerland has joined a "boycott."</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>37 years after fall of Berlin Wall: How divided are Germans?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9434f4307d8eb2af8f868acd63caceb3ca8f2ae52561154db7aff03288b7f0fc</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/37-years-after-fall-of-berlin-wall-how-divided-are-germans/a-79877461--471b79fce1fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/37-years-after-fall-of-berlin-wall-how-divided-are-germans/a-79877461?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three artists share their thoughts on the reunification of East and West Germany. How do they perceive a shared "we" and what gives them cause for optimism?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: CDU names Ilse Aigner as candidate for president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:06d5adad004effa93fb563e78dbc4d409531d84e48a42713c0135134326339d8</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T12:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-cdu-names-ilse-aigner-as-candidate-for-president/a-79898143--f4c7d81c5dcc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-cdu-names-ilse-aigner-as-candidate-for-president/a-79898143?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The steering committtee of the CDU have announced Bavarian politician Ilse Aigner as presidential candidate. This gives her a good chance of becoming the first woman to occupy the role.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU aims to pick new ECB chief by year-end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b1f5be558928df0976fc053da2fd08b9c7bf32b877d1d889eeec293ded608c2</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-aims-to-pick-new-ecb-chief-by-year-end/a-79898169--04bae0a2e38e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-aims-to-pick-new-ecb-chief-by-year-end/a-79898169?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Christine Lagarde's decision to step down early as head of the European Central Bank (ECB) has put the European Union on a tight schedule. The bloc expects to pick a new ECB chief by the end of December.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why Nvidia CEO's affair with alleged Chinese spy matters for AI race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a3c542873ed49846d92e0387fff76dc7400886487e038719bcf53ff547a3a0c</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T11:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-nvidia-ceo-s-affair-with-alleged-chinese-spy-matters-for-ai-race/a-79898338--07d9155781b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-nvidia-ceo-s-affair-with-alleged-chinese-spy-matters-for-ai-race/a-79898338?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang has apologized for an affair with a woman the US believes was spying for China. The story could have profound implications for the world's most valuable company and the global AI race.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Who is Ilse Aigner, leading candidate for Germany's next president?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c71edb6c764ff8257c3579c1cdf31d6beba6fc44a95bab314f59bd011655e6fa</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T11:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-is-ilse-aigner-leading-candidate-for-germany-s-next-president/a-79898848--5540ac90be2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-is-ilse-aigner-leading-candidate-for-germany-s-next-president/a-79898848?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She would be the first female president and the first Christian Social Union politician to hold Germany's highest office. Ilse Aigner is the favored candidate for the Federal Convention vote on January 30.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Germany marks fateful date of November 9</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e47a08799cc2518f1288a31d228f80ec970033a8661f4c3ac88e73f4c9f3cc93</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T07:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-germany-marks-fateful-date-of-november-9/live-79895613--b598062ac50d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-germany-marks-fateful-date-of-november-9/live-79895613?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany is commemorating the Nazi-led November pogroms 88 years ago. Events are also being held to mark the anniversary of the fall of the Berlin Wall in 1989. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Krakow mass shooting suspect has died in hospital, police in Poland say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c2653ff6627c3c41f998e86a2274d48af72911b9b56c357ca388d9354456920</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T06:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/krakow-mass-shooting-suspect-has-died-in-hospital-police-in-poland-say/a-79895626--6dfb07803fa4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/krakow-mass-shooting-suspect-has-died-in-hospital-police-in-poland-say/a-79895626?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The alleged gunman who killed six people in a shooting spree in the Polish city of Krakow has died of injuries sustained in a shootout with police, authorities say.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Chancellor Merz to nominate Aigner for president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72e2c642e62689cb0ee1ef94208bb14ae99e383f06296d65f88b89c77472ed7b</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T19:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-chancellor-merz-to-nominate-aigner-for-president/live-79883533--d347f58eed72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-chancellor-merz-to-nominate-aigner-for-president/live-79883533?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Chancellor Friedrich Merz announced that he will nominate Ilse Aigner for federal president, paving the way for her to be the first woman to hold the office. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'Never Again!': Holocaust remembrance under pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:228e90170c23f60779f2445b6a1399bc7f29ae6c46f4306b0cdc430f9981d18a</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T09:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/never-again-holocaust-remembrance-under-pressure/a-79840894--861f4756e8c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/never-again-holocaust-remembrance-under-pressure/a-79840894?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Only a few Holocaust survivors remain who can share their stories firsthand. Meanwhile, voices calling for an end to what they describe as a "cult of guilt" are growing louder. How can Holocaust remembrance survive?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>As COP31 Antalya kicks off, can world move beyond big promises?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b6d0bb11541b8aa9ac8cf81fce00036a2f92898714343feb1c8d208aa0c6b4d</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T05:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-cop31-antalya-kicks-off-can-world-move-beyond-big-promises/a-79661366--3ff0bee69cef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-cop31-antalya-kicks-off-can-world-move-beyond-big-promises/a-79661366?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Droughts, floods and extreme heat are upping the pressure on delegates at the UN climate talks in Antalya, Turkey. Can countries move beyond pledges to concrete action?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Armenia's selective prosecution: A threat to EU relations?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:900a10a4ca388e2fd066f9848c6f7b4a212a14430f38a6973b0f6d0254af6beb</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T18:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/armenia-s-selective-prosecution-a-threat-to-eu-relations/a-79878159--345ae9a3ae32.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/armenia-s-selective-prosecution-a-threat-to-eu-relations/a-79878159?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While Brussels has refrained from harsh criticism, Armenian civil society has warned of selective justice against opposition figures. Could the EU's pragmatic stance risk repeating past mistakes?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Should AI companies pay for the journalism they use?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7434f98f87561728ecd142f67b5668a6be412e2c9c3182477cd214ec2b081cb7</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T15:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/should-ai-companies-pay-for-the-journalism-they-use/a-79884854--921e36bf95d6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/should-ai-companies-pay-for-the-journalism-they-use/a-79884854?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Publishers say AI chatbots are using their reporting to answer readers' questions while sending back less traffic and less money. Should the companies that build these tools pay for the journalism they rely on?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Son of Iran's shah receives 'Freedom Prize' in Frankfurt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:199955b2ad10c83dff188468bd9b34cdd84d2e8cc47b8a79e3009d7e9f0d55f1</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T14:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/son-of-iran-s-shah-receives-freedom-prize-in-frankfurt/a-79885661--aa99dccac573.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/son-of-iran-s-shah-receives-freedom-prize-in-frankfurt/a-79885661?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">18,000 people gathered in Frankfurt to show support for Reza Pahlavi, the son of the Iranian monarch ousted in 1979. Factions in the opposition have accused him of not distancing himself from his father's rule.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany hopes to host world ice hockey championship — without Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08e34d88bcc48613f18eea07ec5efb61d41079b7b41ad0294c073c9a454b4936</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T11:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-hopes-to-host-world-ice-hockey-championship-without-russia/a-79879536--60661c53ebb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-hopes-to-host-world-ice-hockey-championship-without-russia/a-79879536?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">International protests continue after a court ruled that Russia must be allowed to return to international ice hockey. Germany is seeking a solution that will allow the country to host next year's world championship.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Russia hits Kyiv with airstrikes ahead of trilateral talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:733f4b8078fee50e29bb4f50246b40773445d060467a8b06590ec1cddd3c9515</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T09:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-hits-kyiv-with-airstrikes-ahead-of-trilateral-talks/a-79883851--55817e315a75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-hits-kyiv-with-airstrikes-ahead-of-trilateral-talks/a-79883851?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The strikes hit a major bridge and energy facilities in the Kyiv region. President Volodymyr Zelenskyy accused Moscow of trying to "push" Ukraine "into a blackout" ahead of talks in Abu Dhabi.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Amid protests, France's rising debt costs threaten stability</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d14061876396a03ec9d62ebab1c40fa3469b7f30d55b45c9f95fc14d02c5c23</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/amid-protests-france-s-rising-debt-costs-threaten-stability/a-79865654--50648477f294.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/amid-protests-france-s-rising-debt-costs-threaten-stability/a-79865654?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France plans to spend an extra €4 billion on education amid nationwide protests. But with public debt mounting and interest costs climbing, how much fiscal room does the government have?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Ilse Aigner tipped by party allies as next German president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf83cc3fe1010a7dcfb58937c0acf774a790fce42fe846d5e276512219dc12bb</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T18:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ilse-aigner-tipped-by-party-allies-as-next-german-president/a-79880594--62497