 the war in Ukraine. To sustain their growth, they need to look beyond ammunition and toward new technologies — and even space.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What to know about the IIHF Women's Ice Hockey World Championship</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d8cde217d706948dcd9b9af0907a7bfb28dfed25ec8bcac8d029403e8ff2b50b</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-iihf-women-s-ice-hockey-world-championship/a-79876148--d773b0d8af6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-iihf-women-s-ice-hockey-world-championship/a-79876148?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As ice hockey's governing body continues to wrangle over how to respond to a CAS order to reinstate Russia to international play, the top women's tournament gets underway in Denmark without Russia.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Exercise coaching boosts colon cancer survival</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8fcfd1c60fb53d8d2292f85d77449e815fcda3f8d05c09b425cd71687e89c05c</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T11:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/exercise-coaching-boosts-colon-cancer-survival/a-79856133--6184ce6c4193.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/exercise-coaching-boosts-colon-cancer-survival/a-79856133?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Evidence suggests exercise can keep more cancer patients alive. But what does "living longer" actually mean, and who does it apply to?</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>European shares join a global sell-off as AI spending fears rattle Wall Street and Asian markets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92d44c2a30c421255c52b9900c67278126c51a86084d3632a7d4331658ec137d</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:04Z</updated>